Bob the Tourist is doing extremely well, having recently completed the 
Quest, and made it down to the Castle. Thus far I am genoless, 
polyselfless, and wishless. I'm not crowned, and have all resistances 
except disintegration and possibly cold. I have one magic lamp being used 
as a light source and another blessed magic lamp that could be used for a 
wish. I haven't yet taken on the Castle.

The downside of Bob's situation is equipment. At least 30-40 sacrifices 
have yielded nothing but four-leaf clovers--not a single artifact weapon. 
And I've made it this far without a single piece of core AK material 
(except an AoR and BoH): no speed boots, no DSM, no CoMR, CoDisp, or 
Robe, no magical helms or gauntlets. A polypiling session with all the 
elvish armor and unihorns I could find yielded nothing more interesting 
than a cloak of invisibility (I already had the ring and wands) and a 
spare bag of holding. So I have very mundane equipment, but I'm doing 
well, #twoweaponing a silver saber and a long sword with a +3 ring of 
increase damage, and now I have the PYEC to charge wands and rings.

My dilemma at this point is how to proceed. I'm a bit ticked off at the 
Lady, to tell the truth, and not inclined to continue sacrificing to such 
a parsimonious shrew. I also tend to prefer to use creatively what I find 
along the way, rather than wishing up a perfect AK (I once ascended a 
knight wearing OrangeDSM, for example); on the other hand, I've never had 
a totally wishless ascension either. I've ascended 6 times with various 
classes, so I'm not a newbie but not a pro either. Here are a few ways I 
can think of to proceed (not all mutually exclusive):

Play It Safe -- use the magic lamp to wish for GDSM, take on the Castle, 
get the Castle wand and wish up a good AK. Pros: best chance for 
ascension. Cons: little challenge; typical game.

Focus On Conducts -- keep wishless, genoless, and polyselfless. Perhaps 
continue sacrificing until I do get an artifact weapon. Maybe get dragon 
scales from one of the castle dragons (could reverse genocide, but I 
don't believe I've ID'd the genocide scroll yet, and I have no unholy 
water or magic markers). Pros: it's a nice triple-conduct ascension. 
Cons: I don't actually care about conducts all that much.

Poor Man's Ascension -- I'm rather inclined to see if I could ascend with 
the equipment I have. I seem to be doing quite a bit of damage using 
#twoweapon, and I'm already at AC -19 with several ?oEA and ?oEW waiting 
to be used on AK armor. I could probably get myself near AC -30 with what 
I have. It certainly would be cool to ascend with nothing better than 
mithril and normal enchanted weapons. Pros: great bragging rights, and 
sort of "in character" for a Tourist. Cons: risky, and mithril will 
prevent me from ever using spells effectively.

Spell Slinger -- pry the robe from the cold, dead fingers of the priest 
of Moloch (cursed be he), wish for a helm of brilliance, and start 
studying spells. Pros: I like using spells, and Tourists can advance in 
three categories (although not attack). Cons: *must* swap out metal armor 
before casting becomes practical; therefore this will probably become a 
subset of the Play It Safe strategy.

Any suggestions? Character details follow.


